CAND-0000111,ZPC-000385,,10.1166/jnn.2013.6011,Two-photon induced photopolymerization using photoinitiator with an intramolecular radical quenching moiety for nanolithography,experimental_context,power_measurement_plane=not_reported;resin_formulation=candidate_in_anchor,context,,,,"resulted in the decrease of the weakly-polymerized region, thus the resolution of TPIP was improved. Furthermore, when the photoinitiator had quenching moiety, like BNMBC, was introduced into photoresist, high efﬁciencies of rad- icals quenching and chain terminating could be achieved due to the more collision chances between intramolecu- lar quenching group and radicals in a short time than that of BNBC/PhOCH 3 system, which also led to the higher TPIP resolution. As a result, the narrowest linewidth was obtained from the resin with BNMBC as photoinitiator compared to other photoinitiating systems studied here. 4. CONCLUSIONS In summary, a photoinitiator BNMBC with an intramolec- ular radical quenching group “ p-methoxybenzyl” was investigated in TPIP by comparing with a similar photoini- tiator BNBC without radical quenching group. The TPIP fabrication experiments exhibited that the BNMBC pos- sessed high TPIP initiating efﬁciency and effective radical quenching effect. The linewidth of polymer lines fabri- cated by TPIP of the photoresist using BNMBC as the photoinitiator could be decreased to 65% of those using BNBC. Moreover, this intramolecular radical quenching reaction exhibited more effective conﬁning effect of radi- cal diffusion compared to intermolecular radical quencher with the","resulted in the decrease of the weakly-polymerized region, thus the resolution of TPIP was improved. Furthermore, when the photoinitiator had quenching moiety, like BNMBC, was introduced into photoresist, high efﬁciencies of rad- icals quenching and chain terminating could be achieved due to the more collision chances between intramolecu- lar quenching group and radicals in a short time than that of