CAND-0000114,ZPC-000385,,10.1166/jnn.2013.6011,Two-photon induced photopolymerization using photoinitiator with an intramolecular radical quenching moiety for nanolithography,experimental_context,power_measurement_plane=not_reported;resin_formulation=candidate_in_anchor,context,,,,"e introduced a radical quencher, phenyl methyl ether (PhOCH 3/rparenori, to BNBC and further studied the photopolymerization properties by using BNBC, BNBC/PhOCH 3 and BNMBC as pho- toinitiators with a molar ratio of 0.1%. The results further indicated that BNMBC was effective to conﬁne the radical diffusion in polymerization due to the radical quenching effect of moiety . This intramolecular radical quenching moiety exhibited more effective conﬁning effect of radical diffusion compared to the intermolecular radical quencher PhOCH 3. Furthermore, arbitrary complex three- dimensional (3D) microstructure was achieved using the photoresist with photoinitiator BNMBC. The approach could open up broad prospect for improving the resolution in TPIP . Keywords: T wo-Photon Induced Photopolymerization, Photoinitiator, Radical Quenching Moiety , Nanolithography , Intramolecular Radical Quenching Effect. 1. INTRODUCTION The micro/nanofabrication based on two-photon induced photopolymerization (TPIP) has been extensively studied and established as a powerful and unique tool in the past decade 1/commaori2 due to its particular advantageous for making structures of almost any complexity at the micro/nano scale which was difﬁcult to be achieved using other meth- ods. Recent efforts have been made to improve t","e introduced a radical quencher, phenyl methyl ether (PhOCH 3/rparenori, to BNBC and further studied the photopolymerization properties by using BNBC, BNBC/PhOCH 3 and BNMBC as pho- toinitiators with a molar ratio of 0.1%. The results further indicated that BNMBC was effective to conﬁne the radical diffusion in polymerization due to the radical quenching effect of moiety . This intramolecular radical quenching moiety exhibited more effective conﬁning effect of radical diffusion compared to the intermolecular radical quencher PhOCH 3. Furthermore, arbitrary complex three- dimensional (3D) microstructure was achieved using the photoresist with photoinitiator BNMBC. The approach could open up broad prospect for improving the resolution in TPIP . Keywords: T wo-Photon Induced Photopolymerization, Photoinitiator, Radical Quenching Moiety , Nanolithography , Intramolecular Radical Quenching...",,,,context_candidate,machine_numeric_extraction,machine_medium,auto_retained_context_candidate,automatic_context_or_validation_candidate,two_photon_numeric_extraction,CAND-0000114,,context_missing_wavelength,series context candidate; matched-series equality still requires audit
