CAND-0000142,ZPC-000385,,10.1166/jnn.2013.6011,Two-photon induced photopolymerization using photoinitiator with an intramolecular radical quenching moiety for nanolithography,pi_loading,0.1,%,,,,"LE Lu et al. TPIP Using Photoinitiator with an Intramolecular Radical Quenching Moiety for Nanolithography The dependence of linewidth on the laser power for the two photoresists was shown in Figure 2(a). All the linewidth of the substrate lines were obtained as the aver- age linewidth of ﬁve different regions. R 2 had narrower linewidth than R1 at the same laser power. The linewidth of R1 fabricated at 2.5 mW increased from 221 nm to 703 nm at 9.4 mW. When BNMBC was used as photoini- tiator, the linewidth for R 2 decreased to 154 nm at 2.5 mW and 462 nm at 9.4 mW, respectively. In order to give a clear comparison, we calculated the relative linewidth of R 2 to R1, the values are approximate to 0.67 (Fig. 2(b)) and could be decreased to 0.65 of those using BNBC. The results revealed that the photoresist R 2 containing photoinitiator BNMBC which had a radical quenching group increased the radical termination reaction, thus the linewidth was conﬁned to a smaller range. In order to verify the radical quenching effect of BNMBC from the molecule structure, a radical quencher PhOCH 3 was introduced into BNBC. In addition, we increased the molar ratio of photoinitiator to 0.1% in the resinsR 3,R4 andR5. The polymer lines of R3–R5 were fab- ricated at a laser power of 5.5 mW with the increasing o","width was conﬁned to a smaller range. In order to verify the radical quenching effect of BNMBC from the molecule structure, a radical quencher PhOCH 3 was introduced into BNBC. In addition, we increased the molar ratio of photoinitiator to 0.1% in the resinsR 3,R4 andR5. The polymer lines of R3–R5 were fab- ricated at a laser power of 5.5 mW with the increasing o",,,,numeric_candidate,machine_numeric_extraction,machine_medium,auto_retained_low_context_candidate,automatic_candidate_with_context_warning,two_photon_numeric_extraction,CAND-0000142,,loading_not_normalizable,loading candidate; mmol/g only filled when directly reportable from text
