CAND-0000228,ZPC-001953,,10.1038/s41598-017-17391-1,Additive manufacture of complex 3D Au-containing nanocomposites by simultaneous two-photon polymerisation and photoreduction,voxel_geometry,line_width_um=0.078,mixed,,,,"s the highest efficiency for an initiator in the fabrication of gold-containing composites by two-photon lithography. In this paper, the use of DETC as an efficacious photoinitiator to promote the formation of complex 3D gold-containing nanocomposite structures using simultaneous two-photon polymerisation and photoreduction is shown. It is also demonstrated that the concentration of the gold salt in the resin mixture can be readily varied between 0 and 20 wt%, offering potential for the control of the resultant hybrid microstructure. The feature size can be effectively reduced by incorporation of a gold salt into the resin mixture, with line width as small as 78 nm has been shown to be possible under these conditions. The structural intricacy demonstrated here represents a significant advance in the fabrication complexity achievable. The gold nanoparticles generated in situ exhibit a remarkable optical property of localised surface plasmon resonance (LSPR). The capability demonstrated in this study opens new avenues for a range of applications, including plasmonics, metamaterials, flexible electronics and biosensors. In particularly, user-defined 3D composite structures can be readily fabricated in this way. Results and Discussion A general additive manufacturing (AM) method to","s the highest efficiency for an initiator in the fabrication of gold-containing composites by two-photon lithography. In this paper, the use of DETC as an efficacious photoinitiator to promote the formation of complex 3D gold-containing nanocomposite structures using simultaneous two-photon polymerisation and photoreduction is shown. It is also demonstrated that the concentration of the gold salt in the resin mixture can be readily varied between 0 and 20 wt%, offering potential for the control of the resultant hybrid microstructure. The feature size can be effectively reduced by incorporation of a gold salt into the resin mixture, with line width as small as 78 nm has been shown to be possible under these conditions. The structural intricacy demonstrated here represents a significant advance in the fabrication complexity achievable. The gold nanoparticles generated in situ exhibit a...",,,,context_candidate,machine_numeric_extraction,machine_medium,auto_retained_context_candidate,automatic_context_or_validation_candidate,two_photon_numeric_extraction,CAND-0000228,,COMSOL_context_not_verified,voxel validation candidate; COMSOL readiness requires full optical context
