zotero_95TT3IKI:mechanism:12,zotero_95TT3IKI,95TT3IKI,10.1016/j.jphotochem.2007.03.002,"Synthesis, optical and initiating properties of new two-photon polymerization initiators-2,7-bis(styryl)anthraquinone derivatives",mechanism,,,,,2,"A [6–11]. Plenty of TPIP initiators with large δTPA were reported and showed much higher sensitivity than conventional UV-active initiators. However, most of reported initiators possess high ﬂuorescence quantum yields [12–16].I t means that the probability of radical generation should be low- ered because the relaxation of two-photon induced excited state occurs more via irradiation process than via non-irradiation pro- cess, such as radical generation. Thus, for a TPIP initiator, it is necessary that the molecules not only have large δ TPA, but also possess high capability to efﬁciently produce reactive interme- diate radicals or cations, just like traditional UV initiators [3]. From this","A [6–11]. Plenty of TPIP initiators with large δTPA were reported and showed much higher sensitivity than conventional UV-active initiators. However, most of reported initiators possess high ﬂuorescence quantum yields [12–16].I t means that the probability of radical generation should be low- ered because the relaxation of two-photon induced excited state occurs more via irradiation process than via non-irradiation pro- cess, such as radical generation. Thus, for a TPIP initiator, it is necessary that the molecules not only have large δ TPA, but also possess high capability to efﬁciently produce reactive interme- diate radicals or cations, just like traditional UV initiators [3]. From this",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_95TT3IKI:mechanism:12,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_expansion_20260828/batch_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_95TT3IKI_10.1016_j.jphotochem.2007.03.002.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was