zotero_95TT3IKI:mechanism:13,zotero_95TT3IKI,95TT3IKI,10.1016/j.jphotochem.2007.03.002,"Synthesis, optical and initiating properties of new two-photon polymerization initiators-2,7-bis(styryl)anthraquinone derivatives",mechanism,,,,,2,"ule by intro- ducing electron donor. Here, we select strong electron-donating groups, dimethylamino and methoxy moiety, as donors, and use styryl to prolong π conjugated system. This kind of molecule may possess large δ TPA due to the potential intramolecular charge transfer according to the previous report [11]. Besides large δTPA, these C2v symmetrical molecules often show lower ﬂuorescence quantum yield than those of the linear type [21]. Compounds with low ﬂuorescence quantum yield are preferred for TPIP initiators because low ﬂuorescence quantum yield should guarantee high triplet quantum yield[22–24], which usu- ally leads initiators reacting with monomer to produce radicals or io","ule by intro- ducing electron donor. Here, we select strong electron-donating groups, dimethylamino and methoxy moiety, as donors, and use styryl to prolong π conjugated system. This kind of molecule may possess large δ TPA due to the potential intramolecular charge transfer according to the previous report [11]. Besides large δTPA, these C2v symmetrical molecules often show lower ﬂuorescence quantum yield than those of the linear type [21]. Compounds with low ﬂuorescence quantum yield are preferred for TPIP initiators because low ﬂuorescence quantum yield should guarantee high triplet quantum yield[22–24], which usu- ally leads initiators reacting with monomer to produce radicals or io",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_95TT3IKI:mechanism:13,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_expansion_20260828/batch_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_95TT3IKI_10.1016_j.jphotochem.2007.03.002.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not i