zotero_AU74BQZ6:isc_t1:1,zotero_AU74BQZ6,AU74BQZ6,10.37188/lam.2023.004,Two-photon photopolymerization directly initiated by spiropyran photochromic molecules,isc_t1_proxy,,,,,1,"photopolymerization9. The former can directly generate radical fragments under light irradiation. In contrast, the latter is a two-component photoinitiating system comprising an uncleavable sensitiser and a co-initiator, typically forming excited triplet states under light exposure and requiring a hydrogen donor to react8–11. Researchers are continuously looking for highly effective photoinitiators for different applications, such as titanocene12, squaraine-based initiators13, water-soluble ionic carbazole-based initiators14, substituted thioxanthone- based photoinitiators15, benzylidene cyclopentanones used for one/two-photopolymerizati","photopolymerization9. The former can directly generate radical fragments under light irradiation. In contrast, the latter is a two-component photoinitiating system comprising an uncleavable sensitiser and a co-initiator, typically forming excited triplet states under light exposure and requiring a hydrogen donor to react8–11. Researchers are continuously looking for highly effective photoinitiators for different applications, such as titanocene12, squaraine-based initiators13, water-soluble ionic carbazole-based initiators14, substituted thioxanthone- based photoinitiators15, benzylidene cyclopentanones used for one/two-photopolymerizati",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_AU74BQZ6:isc_t1:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_AU74BQZ6_10.37188_lam.2023.004.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
