zotero_B6B7CEZ3:voxel_geometry:21,zotero_B6B7CEZ3,B6B7CEZ3,10.1021/acsapm.0c01291,Substituted Thioxanthone-Based Photoinitiators for Efficient Two-Photon Direct Laser Writing Polymerization with Two-Color Resolution,voxel_geometry,,,,,7,"powers. This is a clear demonstration of the ability to control the photopolymerization process of the ITX-phenyl-OCH 3 photo- initiator via a secondary light source. These promising lithography results represent a new photoinitiator set tending toward a superresolution capable photoresist system with reduced printing power requirements, which is ideal for high throughput 3D 2PP-DLW. ■ CONCLUSIONS A set of six molecules based on an ITX core was designed and synthesized for use in 2PP-DLW photoinitiator applications. While a desired redshift in absorption was observed for all molecules, those molecules with electron-donating groups exhibited the largest shift toward the target 400 n","powers. This is a clear demonstration of the ability to control the photopolymerization process of the ITX-phenyl-OCH 3 photo- initiator via a secondary light source. These promising lithography results represent a new photoinitiator set tending toward a superresolution capable photoresist system with reduced printing power requirements, which is ideal for high throughput 3D 2PP-DLW. ■ CONCLUSIONS A set of six molecules based on an ITX core was designed and synthesized for use in 2PP-DLW photoinitiator applications. While a desired redshift in absorption was observed for all molecules, those molecules with electron-donating groups exhibited the largest shift toward the target 400 n",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_B6B7CEZ3:voxel_geometry:21,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_B6B7CEZ3_10.1021_acsapm.0c01291.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
