zotero_D6JVVDG4:sigma2:9,zotero_D6JVVDG4,D6JVVDG4,,"An Evidence-Guided, Mechanism-Aware Workflow for Functional Molecular Materials Discovery: Two-Photon Photoinitiators as a Demonstration",sigma_2pa,,,,,3,"models are trained on standardized molecular struc- tures to predict optical and developability-related screening endpoints, and their utility is assessed through scaffold-disjoint testing and literature-basedσ max rank-order com- parisons. Predicted maximum two-photon absorption cross section,σ max, serves as the principal optical ranking signal, whereas model disagreement, applicability-domain status and complementary endpoints are assigned diagnostic or feasibility roles rather than merged into a universal score. Candidates are assigned to mechanism-specific lanes, including single-component Type-I candidates, co-initiator-dependent Type- II candidates and SET/PET exploratory candidates, while cationic","models are trained on standardized molecular struc- tures to predict optical and developability-related screening endpoints, and their utility is assessed through scaffold-disjoint testing and literature-basedσ max rank-order com- parisons. Predicted maximum two-photon absorption cross section,σ max, serves as the principal optical ranking signal, whereas model disagreement, applicability-domain status and complementary endpoints are assigned diagnostic or feasibility roles rather than merged into a universal score. Candidates are assigned to mechanism-specific lanes, including single-component Type-I candidates, co-initiator-dependent Type- II candidates and SET/PET exploratory candidates, while cationic",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_D6JVVDG4:sigma2:9,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_D6JVVDG4.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
zotero_DV89B7W8:isc_t1:4,zotero_DV89B7W8,DV89B7W8,10.2217/rme.13.60,Two-photon polymerization of polyethylene glycol diacrylate scaffolds with riboflavin and triethanolamine used as a water-soluble photoinitiator,isc_t1_proxy,,,,,3,"Flavins have the ability to easily undergo reduction–oxidation reactions, including transport of electrons by FADH 2 in the electron transport chain of cellular respira - tion. Riboflavin is excited by photon absorption and can form either the singlet- or triplet-excited states. It should be noted that the triplet state exhibits a longer lifetime in solution and, as such, is more available for molecular interac - tions than the singlet state. In a nitrogen-purged solution, triplet riboflavin was found to exist for several microseconds after excitation. On the other hand, singlet riboflavin was only observed for 20 ns after excitation [23]. Triplet riboflavin quenched","Flavins have the ability to easily undergo reduction–oxidation reactions, including transport of electrons by FADH 2 in the electron transport chain of cellular respira - tion. Riboflavin is excited by photon absorption and can form either the singlet- or triplet-excited states. It should be noted that the triplet state exhibits a longer lifetime in solution and, as such, is more available for molecular interac - tions than the singlet state. In a nitrogen-purged solution, triplet riboflavin was found to exist for several microseconds after excitation. On the other hand, singlet riboflavin was only observed for 20 ns after excitation [23]. Triplet riboflavin quenched",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_DV89B7W8:isc_t1:4,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_DV89B7W8_10.2217_rme.13.60.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
