zotero_GAG9RQRT:threshold:9,zotero_GAG9RQRT,GAG9RQRT,10.1364/AO.54.007020,"Study of the two-photon excitation of photoinitiator in various solvents, and the two-photon polymerization process",polymerization_threshold,,,,,4,"Fluorescence spectra recorded for single-photon and two- photon excitation are shown in Fig. 7(a). A peak fluorescence signal of approximately 1793 counts at 200 mW laser power was recorded over a 2 s integration time. With 215 μW laser power at 400 nm wavelength, a count of approximately 4537 was obtained with 2 s integration time. The single-photon ab- sorption cross section was calculated from the molar absorption coefficient ε as 43.4 × 10 −18 cm2 molecule−1. The TPA cross section was calculated by comparing fluorescence intensity and was found to be 14 × 10−50 cm4 s photon−1. The main","Fluorescence spectra recorded for single-photon and two- photon excitation are shown in Fig. 7(a). A peak fluorescence signal of approximately 1793 counts at 200 mW laser power was recorded over a 2 s integration time. With 215 μW laser power at 400 nm wavelength, a count of approximately 4537 was obtained with 2 s integration time. The single-photon ab- sorption cross section was calculated from the molar absorption coefficient ε as 43.4 × 10 −18 cm2 molecule−1. The TPA cross section was calculated by comparing fluorescence intensity and was found to be 14 × 10−50 cm4 s photon−1. The main",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_GAG9RQRT:threshold:9,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_GAG9RQRT_10.1364_AO.54.007020.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
zotero_GAG9RQRT:sigma2:1,zotero_GAG9RQRT,GAG9RQRT,10.1364/AO.54.007020,"Study of the two-photon excitation of photoinitiator in various solvents, and the two-photon polymerization process",sigma_2pa,,,,,1,"nnah College for Women, University of Peshawar , Peshawar , Pakistan *Corresponding author: khanalamso@gmail.com Received 26 May 2015; revised 9 July 2015; accepted 15 July 2015; posted 16 July 2015 (Doc. ID 241593); published 6 August 2015 In this study, the two-photon absorption excited fluorescence of the photosensitizer 4,4 0-Bis(diethylamino)ben- zophenonin in different solvents is investigated by using mode-locked Ti:sapphire excitation having a wavelength of 800 nm with pulse duration of 150 fs at the rate of 1 kHz. The fluorescence signals excited by wavelengths of 800 and 400 nm have been compared. Contribution of these cross-section measurements for the two-photon polymerization pro","nnah College for Women, University of Peshawar , Peshawar , Pakistan *Corresponding author: khanalamso@gmail.com Received 26 May 2015; revised 9 July 2015; accepted 15 July 2015; posted 16 July 2015 (Doc. ID 241593); published 6 August 2015 In this study, the two-photon absorption excited fluorescence of the photosensitizer 4,4 0-Bis(diethylamino)ben- zophenonin in different solvents is investigated by using mode-locked Ti:sapphire excitation having a wavelength of 800 nm with pulse duration of 150 fs at the rate of 1 kHz. The fluorescence signals excited by wavelengths of 800 and 400 nm have been compared. Contribution of these cross-section measurements for the two-photon polymerization pro",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_GAG9RQRT:sigma2:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_GAG9RQRT_10.1364_AO.54.007020.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
