zotero_H5G5DD8B:isc_t1:18,zotero_H5G5DD8B,H5G5DD8B,10.1002/polb.24891,Tailored thioxanthone-based photoinitiators for two-photon-controllable polymerization and nanolithographic printing,isc_t1_proxy,,,,,5,"ng mechanism in photopolymerizations is as follows. First, an electron in the ground state (S 0) of ITX is promoted to the ﬁrst excited state (S 1) through a two-photon optical transi- tion using an 800 nm wavelength laser.23 Then, the excited state undergoes intersystem crossing to generate the triplet state (T1), which initiates the polymerization when ITX is blended with the monomeric species. As revealed by previous pump- probe spectroscopy experiments, 12,23 the ITX molecule can undergo depletion of the excited state through both: (a) stimulated-emission depletion (STED) and (b) nonradiative decay by excitation of long-lived species in order to inhibit the polymerization. The latter of","ng mechanism in photopolymerizations is as follows. First, an electron in the ground state (S 0) of ITX is promoted to the ﬁrst excited state (S 1) through a two-photon optical transi- tion using an 800 nm wavelength laser.23 Then, the excited state undergoes intersystem crossing to generate the triplet state (T1), which initiates the polymerization when ITX is blended with the monomeric species. As revealed by previous pump- probe spectroscopy experiments, 12,23 the ITX molecule can undergo depletion of the excited state through both: (a) stimulated-emission depletion (STED) and (b) nonradiative decay by excitation of long-lived species in order to inhibit the polymerization. The latter of",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_H5G5DD8B:isc_t1:18,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_H5G5DD8B_10.1002_polb.24891.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
zotero_H5G5DD8B:isc_t1:3,zotero_H5G5DD8B,H5G5DD8B,10.1002/polb.24891,Tailored thioxanthone-based photoinitiators for two-photon-controllable polymerization and nanolithographic printing,isc_t1_proxy,,,,,1,"improvement in the writing threshold over the commonly used ITX molecule. To elucidate the fundamental mechanism, the excitation and inhibition behavior of the B DAPT molecule were evaluated using density functional theory (DFT) calculations, low-temperature phosphorescence spectroscopy, ultra-fast transient absorption spec- troscopy, and the two-photon Z-scan spectroscopic technique. The improved polymerization threshold of this new photoinitiator pre- sents a clear pathway for the modi ﬁcation of photoinitiators in 3D nanoprinting. © 2019 Wiley Periodicals, Inc. J. Polym. Sci., Part B: Polym. Phys.2019 KEYWORDS: 3D nanoprinting polymerizations; direct laser writ- ing; thioxanthone-ba","improvement in the writing threshold over the commonly used ITX molecule. To elucidate the fundamental mechanism, the excitation and inhibition behavior of the B DAPT molecule were evaluated using density functional theory (DFT) calculations, low-temperature phosphorescence spectroscopy, ultra-fast transient absorption spec- troscopy, and the two-photon Z-scan spectroscopic technique. The improved polymerization threshold of this new photoinitiator pre- sents a clear pathway for the modi ﬁcation of photoinitiators in 3D nanoprinting. © 2019 Wiley Periodicals, Inc. J. Polym. Sci., Part B: Polym. Phys.2019 KEYWORDS: 3D nanoprinting polymerizations; direct laser writ- ing; thioxanthone-ba",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_H5G5DD8B:isc_t1:3,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_H5G5DD8B_10.1002_polb.24891.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
