zotero_H5G5DD8B:threshold:2,zotero_H5G5DD8B,H5G5DD8B,10.1002/polb.24891,Tailored thioxanthone-based photoinitiators for two-photon-controllable polymerization and nanolithographic printing,polymerization_threshold,,,,,1,"ized. Then two-photon polymeriza- tion was performed using the most promising photoinitiating mole- cule. Importantly, one of the initiators, 2,7-bis[(4-(dimethylamino) phenyl ethynyl)-9H-thioxanthen-9-one] (BDAPT), showed a ﬁvefold improvement in the writing threshold over the commonly used ITX molecule. To elucidate the fundamental mechanism, the excitation and inhibition behavior of the B DAPT molecule were evaluated using density functional theory (DFT) calculations, low-temperature phosphorescence spectroscopy, ultra-fast transient absorption spec- troscopy, and the two-photon Z-scan spectroscopic technique. The improved polymerization threshold of this new photoinitiator pre","ized. Then two-photon polymeriza- tion was performed using the most promising photoinitiating mole- cule. Importantly, one of the initiators, 2,7-bis[(4-(dimethylamino) phenyl ethynyl)-9H-thioxanthen-9-one] (BDAPT), showed a ﬁvefold improvement in the writing threshold over the commonly used ITX molecule. To elucidate the fundamental mechanism, the excitation and inhibition behavior of the B DAPT molecule were evaluated using density functional theory (DFT) calculations, low-temperature phosphorescence spectroscopy, ultra-fast transient absorption spec- troscopy, and the two-photon Z-scan spectroscopic technique. The improved polymerization threshold of this new photoinitiator pre",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_H5G5DD8B:threshold:2,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_H5G5DD8B_10.1002_polb.24891.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
