zotero_IMCYIYET:isc_t1:13,zotero_IMCYIYET,IMCYIYET,,Evidence guided mechanism aware workflow for two photon photoinitiator discovery,isc_t1_proxy,,,,,9,"rom the radical headline rather than being mixed into a photoinitiator ranking. Putative Type-I can- didates require evidence for accessible excited-state activation, relevant bond cleavage and chemically credible radical fragments. Type-II candidates require triplet-state characterization and an explicit co-initiator model, because the candidate molecule alone does not define the complete radical-generating system. SET/PET exploratory candidates require donor–acceptor pairing and excited-state electron-transfer thermo- dynamics rather than optical charge-transfer character alone. Quantum-mechanical calculations are therefore used as lane-specific triage rather than as a univers","rom the radical headline rather than being mixed into a photoinitiator ranking. Putative Type-I can- didates require evidence for accessible excited-state activation, relevant bond cleavage and chemically credible radical fragments. Type-II candidates require triplet-state characterization and an explicit co-initiator model, because the candidate molecule alone does not define the complete radical-generating system. SET/PET exploratory candidates require donor–acceptor pairing and excited-state electron-transfer thermo- dynamics rather than optical charge-transfer character alone. Quantum-mechanical calculations are therefore used as lane-specific triage rather than as a univers",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_IMCYIYET:isc_t1:13,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_IMCYIYET.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
