zotero_IMCYIYET:mechanism:2,zotero_IMCYIYET,IMCYIYET,,Evidence guided mechanism aware workflow for two photon photoinitiator discovery,mechanism,,,,,1,"d as sufficient evidence for initiation. Here we present an evidence-guided, mechanism-aware workflow for functional molec- ular materials discovery, demonstrated on radical two-photon photoinitiators. Literature-derived rules define candidate scope, separate Type-I, Type-II and SET/PET candidates from cationic and boundary cases, and constrain six- task molecular learning. Scaffold-isolated tests gave comparable performance for two directed message-passing models (macroR 2 = 0.8415and 0.8411), while benchmark and family audits exposed productive enrichment and OXE-family concentration. Applied to literature-derived derivatives and ZINC22-scale acces- sible space, the workflow","d as sufficient evidence for initiation. Here we present an evidence-guided, mechanism-aware workflow for functional molec- ular materials discovery, demonstrated on radical two-photon photoinitiators. Literature-derived rules define candidate scope, separate Type-I, Type-II and SET/PET candidates from cationic and boundary cases, and constrain six- task molecular learning. Scaffold-isolated tests gave comparable performance for two directed message-passing models (macroR 2 = 0.8415and 0.8411), while benchmark and family audits exposed productive enrichment and OXE-family concentration. Applied to literature-derived derivatives and ZINC22-scale acces- sible space, the workflow",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_IMCYIYET:mechanism:2,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_IMCYIYET.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
