zotero_IMCYIYET:mechanism:8,zotero_IMCYIYET,IMCYIYET,,Evidence guided mechanism aware workflow for two photon photoinitiator discovery,mechanism,,,,,2,"discovery intrinsically mechanism-dependent. A large two-photon absorption cross section increases the prob- ability of excitation, but it does not establish that the excited state will generate radicals capable of initiating polymerization. Single-component Type-I systems require an accessible bond-cleavage pathway and reactive radical fragments. Type-II systems require a suitable hydrogen donor or electron-transfer partner. Donor–acceptor chro- mophores proposed for SET/PET initiation require an energetically credible redox pathway rather than optical charge-transfer character alone. Cationic photoinitia- tors, by contrast, operate through a distinct ionic initiation mechani","discovery intrinsically mechanism-dependent. A large two-photon absorption cross section increases the prob- ability of excitation, but it does not establish that the excited state will generate radicals capable of initiating polymerization. Single-component Type-I systems require an accessible bond-cleavage pathway and reactive radical fragments. Type-II systems require a suitable hydrogen donor or electron-transfer partner. Donor–acceptor chro- mophores proposed for SET/PET initiation require an energetically credible redox pathway rather than optical charge-transfer character alone. Cationic photoinitia- tors, by contrast, operate through a distinct ionic initiation mechani",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_IMCYIYET:mechanism:8,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_IMCYIYET.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
