zotero_IMCYIYET:threshold:7,zotero_IMCYIYET,IMCYIYET,,Evidence guided mechanism aware workflow for two photon photoinitiator discovery,polymerization_threshold,,,,,2,"l, optical and biological functions accessible to 2PP-fabricated materials[1–3]. In this process, the photoini- tiator is not a passive optical absorber; it is the molecular component that couples optical excitation to the radical chemistry governing exposure threshold, writing window and polymerization efficiency[3, 4]. Photoinitiator discovery for 2PP there- fore requires coupled optical and chemical criteria: a useful candidate must absorb efficiently under nonlinear excitation and must also provide a formulation-relevant pathway to productive initiating radicals. This requirement makes two-photon photoinitiator discovery intrinsically mechanism-dependent. A large two-photon ab","l, optical and biological functions accessible to 2PP-fabricated materials[1–3]. In this process, the photoini- tiator is not a passive optical absorber; it is the molecular component that couples optical excitation to the radical chemistry governing exposure threshold, writing window and polymerization efficiency[3, 4]. Photoinitiator discovery for 2PP there- fore requires coupled optical and chemical criteria: a useful candidate must absorb efficiently under nonlinear excitation and must also provide a formulation-relevant pathway to productive initiating radicals. This requirement makes two-photon photoinitiator discovery intrinsically mechanism-dependent. A large two-photon ab",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_IMCYIYET:threshold:7,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_IMCYIYET.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
zotero_IMCYIYET:sigma2:1,zotero_IMCYIYET,IMCYIYET,,Evidence guided mechanism aware workflow for two photon photoinitiator discovery,sigma_2pa,,,,,1,"ution.edu; Abstract Two-photon photoinitiators enable near-infrared three-dimensional microfabri- cation by converting tightly localized excitation into initiating radicals. However, discovery remains concentrated in narrow scaffold series, and high predicted two-photon absorption is often treated as sufficient evidence for initiation. Here we present an evidence-guided, mechanism-aware workflow for functional molec- ular materials discovery, demonstrated on radical two-photon photoinitiators. Literature-derived rules define candidate scope, separate Type-I, Type-II and SET/PET candidates from cationic and boundary cases, and constrain six- task molecular learning. Scaffold-isolated tests gav","ution.edu; Abstract Two-photon photoinitiators enable near-infrared three-dimensional microfabri- cation by converting tightly localized excitation into initiating radicals. However, discovery remains concentrated in narrow scaffold series, and high predicted two-photon absorption is often treated as sufficient evidence for initiation. Here we present an evidence-guided, mechanism-aware workflow for functional molec- ular materials discovery, demonstrated on radical two-photon photoinitiators. Literature-derived rules define candidate scope, separate Type-I, Type-II and SET/PET candidates from cationic and boundary cases, and constrain six- task molecular learning. Scaffold-isolated tests gav",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_IMCYIYET:sigma2:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_IMCYIYET.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
