zotero_INAWB8HL:pi_loading:4,zotero_INAWB8HL,INAWB8HL,10.1115/1.4000097,Process sensitivity analysis and resolution prediction for the two photon polymerization of micro/nano structures,pi_loading,,,,,1,"trol can be signiﬁcantly improved by a good un- derstanding of the synergistic effect of common controlled pro- cess parameters and their effects on the sensitivity of the process resolution. The correct combination of scanning speed, applied laser power, and photoinitiator concentration can signiﬁcantly im- prove the process resolution by reducing the volume where poly- merization reaction propagates. This study presents a comprehensive analysis of the effect of applied process parameters to the resolution of the 2PP process. The objective of this statistical analysis is to evaluate the signiﬁ- cance of commonly employed process parameters to the reso- lution of the 2PP process. A design of experim","trol can be signiﬁcantly improved by a good un- derstanding of the synergistic effect of common controlled pro- cess parameters and their effects on the sensitivity of the process resolution. The correct combination of scanning speed, applied laser power, and photoinitiator concentration can signiﬁcantly im- prove the process resolution by reducing the volume where poly- merization reaction propagates. This study presents a comprehensive analysis of the effect of applied process parameters to the resolution of the 2PP process. The objective of this statistical analysis is to evaluate the signiﬁ- cance of commonly employed process parameters to the reso- lution of the 2PP process. A design of experim",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_INAWB8HL:pi_loading:4,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_expansion_20260828/batch_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_INAWB8HL_10.1115_1.4000097.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted