zotero_LF43QEJD:pi_loading:1,zotero_LF43QEJD,LF43QEJD,10.1109/ICOP56156.2022.9911711,The influence of photoinitiator concentration on the two-photon polymerization threshold of pentaerythritol triacrylate (PETIA) monomer,pi_loading,,,,,1,"The Influence of Photoinitiator Concentration on the Two-Photon Polymerization Threshold of Pentaerythritol Triacrylate (PETIA) Monomer Seyyedhossein Mckee Department of Engineering and Architecture (DIA) University of Parma Parma, Italy seyyedhossein.mckee@unipr.it Adrian H.A. Lutey DIA University of Parma Parma, Italy adrianhughalexander.lutey@unipr.it Corrado Sciancalepore DIA University of Parma Parma, Italy corrado.sciancalepore@unipr.it Federica Poli DIA","The Influence of Photoinitiator Concentration on the Two-Photon Polymerization Threshold of Pentaerythritol Triacrylate (PETIA) Monomer Seyyedhossein Mckee Department of Engineering and Architecture (DIA) University of Parma Parma, Italy seyyedhossein.mckee@unipr.it Adrian H.A. Lutey DIA University of Parma Parma, Italy adrianhughalexander.lutey@unipr.it Corrado Sciancalepore DIA University of Parma Parma, Italy corrado.sciancalepore@unipr.it Federica Poli DIA",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_LF43QEJD:pi_loading:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_LF43QEJD_10.1109_ICOP56156.2022.9911711.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
zotero_LF43QEJD:pi_loading:10,zotero_LF43QEJD,LF43QEJD,10.1109/ICOP56156.2022.9911711,The influence of photoinitiator concentration on the two-photon polymerization threshold of pentaerythritol triacrylate (PETIA) monomer,pi_loading,,,,,3,"IV. C ONCLUSION In this work, the interaction between ultrashort femtosecond pulses of wavelength 515 nm and an acrylate-based ther- mosetting polymer PETIA with three different concentrations of photoinitiator was investigated. Photoinitiator concentration was found to be a fundamental factor which can have a significant influence on the resolution of TPP microfabrication. Therefore, PETIA with 0.2 phr IRGACURE 819 photoini- tiator, namely PETIA (0.2), was identified as the optimum composition, allowing the fabrication of woodpile structures with dimensions of 350 × 350 × 500 µm. ACKNOWLEDGMENT The authors would like to acknowledge funding received from the Emilia-Rom","IV. C ONCLUSION In this work, the interaction between ultrashort femtosecond pulses of wavelength 515 nm and an acrylate-based ther- mosetting polymer PETIA with three different concentrations of photoinitiator was investigated. Photoinitiator concentration was found to be a fundamental factor which can have a significant influence on the resolution of TPP microfabrication. Therefore, PETIA with 0.2 phr IRGACURE 819 photoini- tiator, namely PETIA (0.2), was identified as the optimum composition, allowing the fabrication of woodpile structures with dimensions of 350 × 350 × 500 µm. ACKNOWLEDGMENT The authors would like to acknowledge funding received from the Emilia-Rom",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_LF43QEJD:pi_loading:10,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_LF43QEJD_10.1109_ICOP56156.2022.9911711.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
zotero_LF43QEJD:pi_loading:2,zotero_LF43QEJD,LF43QEJD,10.1109/ICOP56156.2022.9911711,The influence of photoinitiator concentration on the two-photon polymerization threshold of pentaerythritol triacrylate (PETIA) monomer,pi_loading,,,,,1,"In this work, the interaction between 80 femtosecond laser pulses generated with an Ytterbium-doped Potassium Gadolinium Tungstate (Yb:KGW) laser source and a transparent negative photoresist is comprehensively investigated. The results confirm that the photoinitiator concentration directly affects the range of acceptable average laser power, from the polymerization threshold up to the damage threshold, and subsequently the integrity of manufactured structures. Index Terms —3D printing, two-photon polymerization, fem- tosecond laser pulses, photoresist, photoinitiator I. I NTRODUCTION Over recent decades, the rapid advancement of three- dimensional (3D) printing has fundamentally revolutionize","In this work, the interaction between 80 femtosecond laser pulses generated with an Ytterbium-doped Potassium Gadolinium Tungstate (Yb:KGW) laser source and a transparent negative photoresist is comprehensively investigated. The results confirm that the photoinitiator concentration directly affects the range of acceptable average laser power, from the polymerization threshold up to the damage threshold, and subsequently the integrity of manufactured structures. Index Terms —3D printing, two-photon polymerization, fem- tosecond laser pulses, photoresist, photoinitiator I. I NTRODUCTION Over recent decades, the rapid advancement of three- dimensional (3D) printing has fundamentally revolutionize",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_LF43QEJD:pi_loading:2,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_LF43QEJD_10.1109_ICOP56156.2022.9911711.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
