zotero_LF43QEJD:sigma2:7,zotero_LF43QEJD,LF43QEJD,10.1109/ICOP56156.2022.9911711,The influence of photoinitiator concentration on the two-photon polymerization threshold of pentaerythritol triacrylate (PETIA) monomer,sigma_2pa,,,,,2,"II. M ATERIALS AND METHODS A. Photoresist Custom-made negative photoresists, polymerized by free radicals via nonlinear two-photon absorption (TPA), were employed for experiments. Preparation of the photoresists was performed by mixing PETIA (pentaerythritol triacrylate) monomer with 0.1 phr (per hundred resin), 0.2 phr and 0.5 phr IRGACURE 819 (commercial name of the bis(2,4,6- trimethylbenzoyl)-phenylphosphineoxide) photoinitiator until the latter was completely dissolved in the liquid resin monomer. The formulation of each custom photoresist is summari","II. M ATERIALS AND METHODS A. Photoresist Custom-made negative photoresists, polymerized by free radicals via nonlinear two-photon absorption (TPA), were employed for experiments. Preparation of the photoresists was performed by mixing PETIA (pentaerythritol triacrylate) monomer with 0.1 phr (per hundred resin), 0.2 phr and 0.5 phr IRGACURE 819 (commercial name of the bis(2,4,6- trimethylbenzoyl)-phenylphosphineoxide) photoinitiator until the latter was completely dissolved in the liquid resin monomer. The formulation of each custom photoresist is summari",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_LF43QEJD:sigma2:7,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_LF43QEJD_10.1109_ICOP56156.2022.9911711.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
