zotero_LGVQA3RI:sigma2:1,zotero_LGVQA3RI,LGVQA3RI,10.1016/j.eurpolymj.2021.110505,A highly biocompatible bio-ink for 3D hydrogel scaffolds fabrication in the presence of living cells by two-photon polymerization,sigma_2pa,,,,,1,"[20 – 23] . Using a high numerical aperture objective, a femtosecond laser beam can be tightly focused into a photocurable resin consisting of monomers and photoinitiators (PIs). Due to the high density of photons at the focus voxel within a pulse width, two-photon absorption (2PA) of PIs will happen and trigger the polymerization or cross-linking of monomers within the focal volume. More importantly, the energy of a single photon (usually 780 nm) in 2PP is much lower than that of the traditional UV/Vis ones, which can greatly reduce photo damages to the embedded seed cells. In 2013, Liska et al. first reported the 2PP fabrication of 3D hydrogel scaffolds in the presence of human","[20 – 23] . Using a high numerical aperture objective, a femtosecond laser beam can be tightly focused into a photocurable resin consisting of monomers and photoinitiators (PIs). Due to the high density of photons at the focus voxel within a pulse width, two-photon absorption (2PA) of PIs will happen and trigger the polymerization or cross-linking of monomers within the focal volume. More importantly, the energy of a single photon (usually 780 nm) in 2PP is much lower than that of the traditional UV/Vis ones, which can greatly reduce photo damages to the embedded seed cells. In 2013, Liska et al. first reported the 2PP fabrication of 3D hydrogel scaffolds in the presence of human",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_LGVQA3RI:sigma2:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_LGVQA3RI_10.1016_j.eurpolymj.2021.110505.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
