zotero_MZLGYQTP:sigma2:2,zotero_MZLGYQTP,MZLGYQTP,10.1016/j.jphotochem.2009.02.007,A water-soluble two-photon photopolymerization initiation system: Methylated-β-cyclodextrin complex of xanthene dye/aryliodonium salt,sigma_2pa,,,,,1,"e TPA materials were success- fully developed in biological imaging[14–16] . Very few articles have focused on water-soluble two-photon polymerization (TPP)[12,13]. The rate of photopolymerization is mainly inﬂuenced by two parameters in TPP: (i) multi-photon absorption cross-section, which provides the probability of multi-photon absorption at a par- ticular frequency and (ii) quantum yield of generated radicals or ions, and the initiation of efﬁciency of the generated radicals and ions [1 7]. Designing and synthesizing large cross-section, water- soluble TPA dyes is difﬁcult. Development of a simple method to ∗ Corresponding author. Fax: +86 10 82375712. E-mail address: lidong@mater.ustb.edu.c","e TPA materials were success- fully developed in biological imaging[14–16] . Very few articles have focused on water-soluble two-photon polymerization (TPP)[12,13]. The rate of photopolymerization is mainly inﬂuenced by two parameters in TPP: (i) multi-photon absorption cross-section, which provides the probability of multi-photon absorption at a par- ticular frequency and (ii) quantum yield of generated radicals or ions, and the initiation of efﬁciency of the generated radicals and ions [1 7]. Designing and synthesizing large cross-section, water- soluble TPA dyes is difﬁcult. Development of a simple method to ∗ Corresponding author. Fax: +86 10 82375712. E-mail address: lidong@mater.ustb.edu.c",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_MZLGYQTP:sigma2:2,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_expansion_20260828/batch_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_MZLGYQTP_10.1016_j.jphotochem.2009.02.007.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extracti