zotero_PJQEIM6F:pi_loading:1,zotero_PJQEIM6F,PJQEIM6F,10.1021/acsapm.4c00932,Heteroatom/Heterocycle-Substituted Ketone Dyes as Efficient Photoinitiators in Visible Light-Emitting Diode/Near Infrared Light Photopolymerization with Enhanced Two-Photon Lithography Capability,pi_loading,,,,,1,"ts the most excellent light absorption properties as well as the fastest reaction efficiency with amine additives. Notably, when comparing the two-photon lithography capability, the photoresist containing 0.1 wt % CCK− Th, which can achieve a writing speed of 46 mm s −1 , exhibits high two-photon sensitivity, about two times that of the benzene ring- substituted CCK−Ben. In addition, CCK−Th shows outstanding ability to construct complex three-dimensional patterns. These modified CCKs show great application potential in nanotechnology, additive manufacturing, and optoelectronics and provide design concepts for the development of photoinitiators. KEYWORDS: Photopolymerization, T","ts the most excellent light absorption properties as well as the fastest reaction efficiency with amine additives. Notably, when comparing the two-photon lithography capability, the photoresist containing 0.1 wt % CCK− Th, which can achieve a writing speed of 46 mm s −1 , exhibits high two-photon sensitivity, about two times that of the benzene ring- substituted CCK−Ben. In addition, CCK−Th shows outstanding ability to construct complex three-dimensional patterns. These modified CCKs show great application potential in nanotechnology, additive manufacturing, and optoelectronics and provide design concepts for the development of photoinitiators. KEYWORDS: Photopolymerization, T",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_PJQEIM6F:pi_loading:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_PJQEIM6F_10.1021_acsapm.4c00932.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was