zotero_PJQEIM6F:sigma2:12,zotero_PJQEIM6F,PJQEIM6F,10.1021/acsapm.4c00932,Heteroatom/Heterocycle-Substituted Ketone Dyes as Efficient Photoinitiators in Visible Light-Emitting Diode/Near Infrared Light Photopolymerization with Enhanced Two-Photon Lithography Capability,sigma_2pa,,,,,7,"Both molecules have large TPA cross-section, predicting their considerable performance in two-photon lithography. The TPA cross-section of CCK-Th (δ 780 nm = 425 GM) is higher than that of CCK-Ben (δ 780 nm = 343 GM), which can be attributed to the stronger light-absorbing property of the former. Although adding MDEA will increase the sensitivity of the molecule in two-photon lithography, it will reduce the fineness of the lines (Figure S6). Since such molecules have both carbonyl and α-aminoalkyl groups, they can be used alone as one-component type II PIs, which are also effec","Both molecules have large TPA cross-section, predicting their considerable performance in two-photon lithography. The TPA cross-section of CCK-Th (δ 780 nm = 425 GM) is higher than that of CCK-Ben (δ 780 nm = 343 GM), which can be attributed to the stronger light-absorbing property of the former. Although adding MDEA will increase the sensitivity of the molecule in two-photon lithography, it will reduce the fineness of the lines (Figure S6). Since such molecules have both carbonyl and α-aminoalkyl groups, they can be used alone as one-component type II PIs, which are also effec",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_PJQEIM6F:sigma2:12,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_PJQEIM6F_10.1021_acsapm.4c00932.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
