zotero_QH8XLKS5:voxel_geometry:1,zotero_QH8XLKS5,QH8XLKS5,10.1016/j.polymer.2017.04.039,Localized polymerization using single photon photoinitiators in two photon process for fabricating subwavelength structures,voxel_geometry,,,,,1,"roprietary. L TPO-L is an inexpensive, easily available single photon photoinitiator and has been used extensively for single photon absorption of UV light for polymerization. These polymerization volumes however are not localized and extend to micron size resolution having limited applications . We have exploited high quantum yield of radicals of LTPO-Lfor absorption of two photons to achieve localized polymerization in subwavelength volumes, much below the diffraction limi t. Critical concentration (10wt%) of LTPO- Lin acrylate (Sartomer) was found optimal to achieve subwavelength localized poly merization and has been demonstrated by fabricating 2D/3D complex nanostruct","roprietary. L TPO-L is an inexpensive, easily available single photon photoinitiator and has been used extensively for single photon absorption of UV light for polymerization. These polymerization volumes however are not localized and extend to micron size resolution having limited applications . We have exploited high quantum yield of radicals of LTPO-Lfor absorption of two photons to achieve localized polymerization in subwavelength volumes, much below the diffraction limi t. Critical concentration (10wt%) of LTPO- Lin acrylate (Sartomer) was found optimal to achieve subwavelength localized poly merization and has been demonstrated by fabricating 2D/3D complex nanostruct",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_QH8XLKS5:voxel_geometry:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_QH8XLKS5_10.1016_j.polymer.2017.04.039.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
