zotero_RK5TXPZ5:sigma2:2,zotero_RK5TXPZ5,RK5TXPZ5,10.1364/OE.6.000064,Two-photon holography in 3-D photopolymer host-guest matrix,sigma_2pa,,,,,2,"ave been explored: 1) recording in a high viscosity liquid photopolymerizable formulation; 2) recording in polymeric host filled with a liquid photopolymerizable formulation. In both cases Benzil- Di-Methyl-Ketal (BDMK) was used as two-photon photoinitiator, two-photon absorption of which is enhanced due to extended structural features of the molecule, in particular side- methyl groups located between two benzene rings. The employed wavelength of 710 nm is far away from the nearest absorption band, favoring no single photon excitation at 710 nm but rather a two-photon excitation transition at 355 nm. This photoinitiator has been measured to have a two-photon threshold in DPEPA (Di-Penta-Ery","ave been explored: 1) recording in a high viscosity liquid photopolymerizable formulation; 2) recording in polymeric host filled with a liquid photopolymerizable formulation. In both cases Benzil- Di-Methyl-Ketal (BDMK) was used as two-photon photoinitiator, two-photon absorption of which is enhanced due to extended structural features of the molecule, in particular side- methyl groups located between two benzene rings. The employed wavelength of 710 nm is far away from the nearest absorption band, favoring no single photon excitation at 710 nm but rather a two-photon excitation transition at 355 nm. This photoinitiator has been measured to have a two-photon threshold in DPEPA (Di-Penta-Ery",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_RK5TXPZ5:sigma2:2,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_expansion_20260828/batch_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_RK5TXPZ5_10.1364_OE.6.000064.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
zotero_RK5TXPZ5:voxel_geometry:7,zotero_RK5TXPZ5,RK5TXPZ5,10.1364/OE.6.000064,Two-photon holography in 3-D photopolymer host-guest matrix,voxel_geometry,,,,,4,"patial overlap of the two pulses. Fringe spacing is approximately 2 µm, and can be modified by adjusting Δx. The zigzag pattern is because of the presence of vibrations due to the coupling of the cooling pump of the argon laser to the table. Ultimate spatial resolution of two-photon holographic gratings is limited by the amount of polymerization outside the illuminated regions, however, because of the nonlinear threshold of the two-photon process, fringe spacing can be smaller than in one- photon holographic gratings, effectively at the polymer chain diffusion limit. [9] Diffraction efficiency (D.E.) of holograms made in liquid and in solid gel was measured. Holograms made in liqu","patial overlap of the two pulses. Fringe spacing is approximately 2 µm, and can be modified by adjusting Δx. The zigzag pattern is because of the presence of vibrations due to the coupling of the cooling pump of the argon laser to the table. Ultimate spatial resolution of two-photon holographic gratings is limited by the amount of polymerization outside the illuminated regions, however, because of the nonlinear threshold of the two-photon process, fringe spacing can be smaller than in one- photon holographic gratings, effectively at the polymer chain diffusion limit. [9] Diffraction efficiency (D.E.) of holograms made in liquid and in solid gel was measured. Holograms made in liqu",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_RK5TXPZ5:voxel_geometry:7,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_expansion_20260828/batch_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_RK5TXPZ5_10.1364_OE.6.000064.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
