zotero_RU8URT2Z:mechanism:1,zotero_RU8URT2Z,RU8URT2Z,,Mechanism aware discovery of radical two photon photoinitiators from accessible chemical space,mechanism,,,,,1,"reening rules, combines paired multitask molecular prediction models with applicability-domain and model-disagreement analyses, and advances can- didate families through mechanism-specific quantum-chemical evaluation. This framework separates single-component Type-I candidates from co-initiator- dependent Type-II and SET/PET boundary cases, preventing optical-property prediction from being overinterpreted as photoinitiation evidence. The result is a traceable prioritization strategy that transforms broad virtual chemical space into experimentally testable, mechanism-qualified candidate families. Keywords:two-photon polymerization; photoinitiator discovery; molecular machine lea","reening rules, combines paired multitask molecular prediction models with applicability-domain and model-disagreement analyses, and advances can- didate families through mechanism-specific quantum-chemical evaluation. This framework separates single-component Type-I candidates from co-initiator- dependent Type-II and SET/PET boundary cases, preventing optical-property prediction from being overinterpreted as photoinitiation evidence. The result is a traceable prioritization strategy that transforms broad virtual chemical space into experimentally testable, mechanism-qualified candidate families. Keywords:two-photon polymerization; photoinitiator discovery; molecular machine lea",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_RU8URT2Z:mechanism:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_RU8URT2Z.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
