zotero_TN4FRK7S:mechanism:3,zotero_TN4FRK7S,TN4FRK7S,10.1080/15685551.2015.1092008,Synthesis of new photoactive urethane carbohydrates and their behavior in UV or femtosecond laser-induced two-photon polymerization,mechanism,,,,,7,"hotopolymerization behavior 3.2.1. Effect of photoinitiators A versatile and widely applied technique for the polymeriza- tion of (meth)acrylates is their exposure to UV radiation in the presence of free radical initiators, which can be described as either ‘hydrogen abstraction type’ or ‘alpha cleavage type’ . The alpha cleavage initiators have usually a higher efficiency due to the generation of free radicals via a unimolecular process, while the hydrogen abstraction initiators lead to free radicals through a bimolecular process. In line with these features, Figure 4. evolution of the double bond absorption band at 815 cm −1 from the formulations a1 (a) and B1 (b) monitored as a fun","hotopolymerization behavior 3.2.1. Effect of photoinitiators A versatile and widely applied technique for the polymeriza- tion of (meth)acrylates is their exposure to UV radiation in the presence of free radical initiators, which can be described as either ‘hydrogen abstraction type’ or ‘alpha cleavage type’ . The alpha cleavage initiators have usually a higher efficiency due to the generation of free radicals via a unimolecular process, while the hydrogen abstraction initiators lead to free radicals through a bimolecular process. In line with these features, Figure 4. evolution of the double bond absorption band at 815 cm −1 from the formulations a1 (a) and B1 (b) monitored as a fun",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_TN4FRK7S:mechanism:3,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_TN4FRK7S_10.1080_15685551.2015.1092008.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
