zotero_TN4FRK7S:voxel_geometry:1,zotero_TN4FRK7S,TN4FRK7S,10.1080/15685551.2015.1092008,Synthesis of new photoactive urethane carbohydrates and their behavior in UV or femtosecond laser-induced two-photon polymerization,voxel_geometry,,,,,3,"The application of a locally controlled polymerization (2PP) allows the creation of precisely defined structures, which could not be generated by means of tradi- tional photolithography approaches. This advantage can be exploited in the fabrication of high-resolution 3D biomimetic structures (filamentous substrates for cardiac tissue, trabec- ular-like scaffolds, bio-inspired artificial blood vessels, and other bioapplications).[38–41] Generally, the photocurable materials for 2PP are acrylates and epoxy derivatives based on poly(ethylene glycol) and organically modified silicates.[42– 44] Recently, scaffolds containing acrylated polysaccharides, namely hyaluronan–glycidyl","The application of a locally controlled polymerization (2PP) allows the creation of precisely defined structures, which could not be generated by means of tradi- tional photolithography approaches. This advantage can be exploited in the fabrication of high-resolution 3D biomimetic structures (filamentous substrates for cardiac tissue, trabec- ular-like scaffolds, bio-inspired artificial blood vessels, and other bioapplications).[38–41] Generally, the photocurable materials for 2PP are acrylates and epoxy derivatives based on poly(ethylene glycol) and organically modified silicates.[42– 44] Recently, scaffolds containing acrylated polysaccharides, namely hyaluronan–glycidyl",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_TN4FRK7S:voxel_geometry:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_TN4FRK7S_10.1080_15685551.2015.1092008.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
