zotero_U5ZNIGNS:sigma2:1,zotero_U5ZNIGNS,U5ZNIGNS,10.1039/c8me00101d,Towards efficient initiators for two-photon induced polymerization: fine tuning of the donor/acceptor properties,sigma_2pa,,,,,2,"ity. The maximum 2PA cross sections prove to be strongly dependent on the nature of the TPA substituent and range between ∼ 173 GM (Goeppert-Mayer units) and 379 GM. Although most of the investi- gated substances also exhibit high fluorescence quantum yields, two-photon absorption screening tests of an acrylate monomer formulation revealed the efficiency of these materials as 2PA photoinitiators. These re- sults are supported by quantum chemical calculations of the spin density distribution indicating that the mechanism of polymerization initiation using acrylate monomer is favored by strong localization of the un- paired electrons in the triplet state on the C2 carbon of the thiophene moiety","ity. The maximum 2PA cross sections prove to be strongly dependent on the nature of the TPA substituent and range between ∼ 173 GM (Goeppert-Mayer units) and 379 GM. Although most of the investi- gated substances also exhibit high fluorescence quantum yields, two-photon absorption screening tests of an acrylate monomer formulation revealed the efficiency of these materials as 2PA photoinitiators. These re- sults are supported by quantum chemical calculations of the spin density distribution indicating that the mechanism of polymerization initiation using acrylate monomer is favored by strong localization of the un- paired electrons in the triplet state on the C2 carbon of the thiophene moiety",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_U5ZNIGNS:sigma2:1,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_U5ZNIGNS_10.1039_c8me00101d.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
