zotero_V8BAREKK:voxel_geometry:4,zotero_V8BAREKK,V8BAREKK,10.1039/d2tc00331g,Geometry-driven mass transport dynamics within permeable 3D-microstructures fabricated via two-photon polymerization,voxel_geometry,,,,,3,"2 1. INTRODUCTION. Two-photon polymerization (2PP) constitutes one of the most promising maskless stereolithography technologies1-3 allowing the production of truly 3D-structures with high spatial resolution. The generated 3D-architectures can display a very high degree of structural details which are tailored specifically using a very flexible computing assisted parameterization which is now routinely proposed in commercially available two-photon 3D-printing systems4. From a fundamental point of view, the exceptional high writing accuracy of 2PP is achieved by tightly focusing of a fs-pulse laser into the photoactive m","2 1. INTRODUCTION. Two-photon polymerization (2PP) constitutes one of the most promising maskless stereolithography technologies1-3 allowing the production of truly 3D-structures with high spatial resolution. The generated 3D-architectures can display a very high degree of structural details which are tailored specifically using a very flexible computing assisted parameterization which is now routinely proposed in commercially available two-photon 3D-printing systems4. From a fundamental point of view, the exceptional high writing accuracy of 2PP is achieved by tightly focusing of a fs-pulse laser into the photoactive m",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_V8BAREKK:voxel_geometry:4,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_V8BAREKK_10.1039_d2tc00331g.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
