zotero_X4RTKEJL:threshold:3,zotero_X4RTKEJL,X4RTKEJL,10.1088/1758-5082/3/2/025003,Fabrication of 2D protein microstructures and 3D polymer-protein hybrid microstructures by two-photon polymerization,polymerization_threshold,,,,,3,"n method able to generate porous protein-based scaffolds with high micro- and nanostructure control is two-photon polymerization (TPP). Here, an ultrashort pulsed laser beam is tightly focused by a microscope objective generating laser intensities exceeding a threshold to initiate nonlinear absorption processes [ 8]. These absorption processes initiate a crosslinking inside a pre-polymeric bath, which can be used to generate microstructures with a resolution below the diffraction limit of the focusing objective. TPP is applicable to a number of different photosensitive polymers, such as inelastic polymers like SU-8 (e.g. [ 9]), elastic polymers like poly(dimethylsiloxan) PDMS (e.g","n method able to generate porous protein-based scaffolds with high micro- and nanostructure control is two-photon polymerization (TPP). Here, an ultrashort pulsed laser beam is tightly focused by a microscope objective generating laser intensities exceeding a threshold to initiate nonlinear absorption processes [ 8]. These absorption processes initiate a crosslinking inside a pre-polymeric bath, which can be used to generate microstructures with a resolution below the diffraction limit of the focusing objective. TPP is applicable to a number of different photosensitive polymers, such as inelastic polymers like SU-8 (e.g. [ 9]), elastic polymers like poly(dimethylsiloxan) PDMS (e.g",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_X4RTKEJL:threshold:3,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_X4RTKEJL_10.1088_1758-5082_3_2_025003.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
