zotero_X4RTKEJL:sigma2:2,zotero_X4RTKEJL,X4RTKEJL,10.1088/1758-5082/3/2/025003,Fabrication of 2D protein microstructures and 3D polymer-protein hybrid microstructures by two-photon polymerization,sigma_2pa,,,,,3,"setup. In order to further facilitate the future use of TPP in biofabrication applications, in this study we tested and compared the polymerization efﬁciency of fs- and ps-systems on several synthetic and biological materials. A novel photoinitiator with high two-photon absorption capabilities in the visible range was synthesized to increase the polymerization efﬁciency. 3D microstructures fabricated with a ps-system and a fs-system and examples of polymer– protein hybrid structures are presented. The tissue engineering capabilities of TPP were demonstrated by the analysis of chondrocyte growth on cross-linked gelatin microlines. 2. Materials and methods 2.1. Material systems 2.1.1. Synthesis","setup. In order to further facilitate the future use of TPP in biofabrication applications, in this study we tested and compared the polymerization efﬁciency of fs- and ps-systems on several synthetic and biological materials. A novel photoinitiator with high two-photon absorption capabilities in the visible range was synthesized to increase the polymerization efﬁciency. 3D microstructures fabricated with a ps-system and a fs-system and examples of polymer– protein hybrid structures are presented. The tissue engineering capabilities of TPP were demonstrated by the analysis of chondrocyte growth on cross-linked gelatin microlines. 2. Materials and methods 2.1. Material systems 2.1.1. Synthesis",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_X4RTKEJL:sigma2:2,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_X4RTKEJL_10.1088_1758-5082_3_2_025003.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
