zotero_X4RTKEJL:voxel_geometry:7,zotero_X4RTKEJL,X4RTKEJL,10.1088/1758-5082/3/2/025003,Fabrication of 2D protein microstructures and 3D polymer-protein hybrid microstructures by two-photon polymerization,voxel_geometry,,,,,5,"Biofabrication 3 (2011) 025003 S Engelhardt et al 2.4. Determination of polymerization efﬁciency The polymerization efﬁciency of the different materials and irradiation conditions was determined by measuring the growth of voxels (volume pixel), since voxels are a direct representation of the polymerization procedure. For this reason, the ascending voxel method was used [35]. Irradiation starts within the glass slide and the vertical position is increased 100 nm with each voxel, until the voxels are no longer attached to the surface and begin to ﬂoat away. Therefore, the voxel length can be directly measured by counting the number of voxels","Biofabrication 3 (2011) 025003 S Engelhardt et al 2.4. Determination of polymerization efﬁciency The polymerization efﬁciency of the different materials and irradiation conditions was determined by measuring the growth of voxels (volume pixel), since voxels are a direct representation of the polymerization procedure. For this reason, the ascending voxel method was used [35]. Irradiation starts within the glass slide and the vertical position is increased 100 nm with each voxel, until the voxels are no longer attached to the surface and begin to ﬂoat away. Therefore, the voxel length can be directly measured by counting the number of voxels",,,,anchor_candidate,machine_text_anchor,text_exact_candidate,auto_anchor_candidate,automatic_field_discovery,anchor_mining,zotero_X4RTKEJL:voxel_geometry:7,outputs/zotero_tpp_literature_pilot_20260828/parsed_local_pdfs/texts/zotero_X4RTKEJL_10.1088_1758-5082_3_2_025003.txt,Keyword/field anchor mined from parsed full text; value extraction was not independently asserted.,pending
